   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disability equity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Kiribati Disability Support Program is an investment that supports the Kiribati School and Centre for Children with Disabilities (KSCCD) to provide educational services to children with disabilities.  The investment aim is to enable KSCCD&#x2019;s registration as a school with the Ministry of Education (MoE) to better access government funding. To meet the requirements of registration, Australia has supported KSCCD to strengthen organisational capacity related to financial management and governance through provision of training, policy development and mentoring from
&#x200d;
Australian volunteers. In the reporting period, KSCCD demonstrated significant improvements in organisational capacity, for example, KSCCD is now fully meeting its obligations under the grant agreement by submitting quality and timely financial reports. This has resulted in tranche payments and reporting being reduced to. 6 six-monthly rather than every second month. KSCCD is now also compliant with MoE requirements and has applied for registration as a school.</narrative>
    </description>
